1. [BLOCKER] phases/phase-061/REPORT.md:168-169 — The Gates table is unfilled: `cargo test --all-targets | TEST_TOTAL_PLACEHOLDER` and `../rbops/verify.sh phase-061 | VERIFY_PLACEHOLDER`. The report ships with the two gates that decide the phase carrying no result at all — this is not a claim of a pass, it is an absent claim, which the pipeline cannot distinguish from a pass. Fix: run both and record the real numbers (e.g. `test result: ok. N passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored` and verify.sh's own line) before the phase ships.
2. [MAJOR] phases/phase-061/REPORT.md:86 — "This run's diff (`0e84349..HEAD` plus the working tree) is the acknowledgement row above, **+1 line, 1 file**." It is not: `git diff --numstat` is `230 0 phases/phase-061/REPORT.md`, `69 19 src/repl/mod.rs`, `1 0 tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs`. The run made a behavioural change to `edit_in` (the scratch-file cleanup at src/repl/mod.rs:2385-2414) and added `edge_a_failed_edit_leaves_no_copy_of_the_buffer_behind` (src/repl/mod.rs:6187), and neither appears in the "What changed" table (REPORT.md:90-97) nor in the "Tests added" table, whose 16 rows contain no such test. The `resource_limit` row at REPORT.md:198 still justifies cleanup with the success-path test alone. Fix: rewrite the "What changed" and "Tests added" tables against `git diff 0e84349`, and update the `resource_limit` row to cite the new test.
3. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2332 — `self.tutorial_step = Some(0)` is the only write to that field anywhere in the tree (the other hits are the declaration at 648, the `None` init at 667, the read at 2337, and tests). Nothing ever advances it, so `show_hint` answers "step 1 of 6" forever: `hint_lines`'s `Some` arm at src/repl/mod.rs:475 is unreachable with an index above 0, and `TUTORIAL[1..6].hint` is dead data. Yet `:help` advertises "Hint for the tutorial step this session is on" (src/repl/commands.rs:449) and the tour footer prints "Type :hint for the step you are on" (src/repl/mod.rs:465). `a_hint_in_the_tour_names_the_step_it_is_for` (src/repl/mod.rs:6047-6065) asserts only `Some(0)`, so it pins the single reachable value and cannot fail on this. Fix: advance in `execute_code_from` when the executed code matches the current step's `snippet`, or change the help text and the footer to say the first step's hint is the one given.
4. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:6119 — `edge_edit_without_an_editor_names_the_variable_and_keeps_the_buffer` asserts `repl.in_multiline` and `repl.multiline_buffer` are unchanged across a call to `edit_in`, which takes `&self` (src/repl/mod.rs:2363) and therefore cannot touch them. The assertion is enforced by the borrow checker, not by the code — the exact "test that cannot fail" class REPORT.md:150-153 presents as its evidence that "**A failure is asserted**, not only successes". The same tautology repeats at src/repl/mod.rs:6146-6150 and 6171-6175. Fix: drive the `&mut self` entry point (`edit_buffer`, src/repl/mod.rs:2419) with the editor injected as a parameter rather than read from the process environment, and assert the buffer there.
5. [MAJOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2378 — The scratch file is `std::env::temp_dir().join(format!("redblue-edit-{}.rb", std::process::id()))`, written with `std::fs::write` (2382) into a world-writable shared directory, with no random component, no `create_new`, and no `O_NOFOLLOW`. `fs::write` follows symlinks and truncates: any other local user who can guess the pid can pre-create `/tmp/redblue-edit-<pid>.rb` as a symlink and the session will write the reader's buffer through it into any file the invoking user can write, and hand that path to `$EDITOR`. The file is also created 0o644 (umask), so the buffer is world-readable for the lifetime of the edit. Fix: `create_dir` a private directory under `temp_dir()` and create the file inside it with `OpenOptions::new().write(true).create_new(true)` and mode 0o600.
6. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:476 — `hint_lines` takes `style` and uses it only in the `None` arm (482-486); the in-tour answer at 476-481 is returned unpainted, so within one command the "there is no tutorial step" text is coloured and the actual hint is not. `edge_a_painted_hint_keeps_the_hint_readable` (src/repl/mod.rs:6263) passes `hint_lines(None, ...)` only, so the un-painted arm is uncovered — REPORT.md:157 ("the painted hint is the plain hint painted, and nothing else") describes the branch that is never taken in the tour. Fix: paint the `Some` arm with `style.paint(Paint::Heading, ...)` and extend the test to `Some(0)`.
7. [MINOR] src/repl/editor.rs:891 — `edge_members_and_paths_do_not_fight_over_one_tab` asserts the bare-dot answer equals `stdlib::MODULES` in declaration order, while `complete_dotted` sorts (src/repl/completer.rs:250). It passes only because `MODULES` happens to be declared alphabetically (src/stdlib.rs:20); reordering that unrelated table would fail this test with no behaviour change. Fix: sort the expected vector before comparing.
8. [MINOR] src/repl/mod.rs:2424 — On the success path `edit_buffer` clears `multiline_buffer` and `in_multiline` *before* `execute_code(&edited)`. A block the editor wrote that fails to parse or analyze is discarded with no way back — the only route into a session for a long block destroys it on a typo. The doc at 2417-2418 promises preservation only "when the editor could not be opened at all". Fix: capture the result from `execute_code` and push `edited` back into `multiline_buffer` when it is an `Err`.
9. [MINOR] src/repl/editor.rs:231 — The `out_of_bounds` edge row (REPORT.md:191) is claimed to be covered by `signature_hint("say split(", 5)` being "`None`, not a slice panic". It is not a bounds case: `5` is inside the line, `line.get(..5)` succeeds and returns `"say s"`, and the `None` comes from `strip_suffix('(')` at line 232. The guard the row is about — `pos` past the end, or `pos` mid-character returning `None` — is never exercised. Fix: add `signature_hint("say split(", 999)` and a multi-byte case with `pos` inside the character.
10. [STYLE] src/repl/mod.rs:495 — `step_index` recovers an index by `std::ptr::eq` over the `'static` table and `.unwrap_or(0)`, silently answering "step 1" for a step that is not in the table, while `hint_lines` already holds the index in the `Some` binding at line 475. Dead indirection with a silent-wrong-answer default; use the index directly.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 10
